WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Spare Room: run the recruiter's code in a room with nothing in it.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.500
Binance's $6.34B loss involved an engineer running a recruiter's coding assignment on his work computer.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.426
Your account: the one you use every day, with your keys, logins and wallets.

4
00:00:13.426 --> 00:00:21.104
Spare Room's scan of a bundled fake laptop: 25 things code running as you could reach. It never reads their contents.

5
00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:28.351
The same results as a local report. It loads nothing from the internet.

6
00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:36.845
The check a stranger's code could make, against 13 fake secrets in your folder: all 13 reachable.

7
00:00:36.845 --> 00:00:42.845
Creating the spare room took 29.6 s (recorded earlier; Windows does not allow its permission prompt to be screen-recorded).

8
00:00:42.845 --> 00:00:45.760
The spare room: a separate, standard Windows account with nothing in it.

9
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:54.152
Can the coding test run here? Node.js, npm and Git, yes. Python and VS Code need installing for all users.

10
00:00:54.152 --> 00:01:02.349
The same 13 paths, tried from the spare room: 13 blocked.

11
00:01:02.349 --> 00:01:10.928
Checked from inside: none of the 12 secret locations in your account are readable. One .env outside any account folder still is.

12
00:01:10.928 --> 00:01:17.428
13 reachable, then 0. Offline. Never reads secret contents. Weaker than a virtual machine. spare-room-demo.netlify.app
